<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Task>
    <Title>Config - RES ONE Workspace Top Level Relay - Reset Credentials - Windows</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<DIV id=fixletMessage2 class=FixletMessage>
<DIV id=paramFixletDescription>
<P>This parameterized Fixlet allows you to reconfigure RES ONE Workspace Top Level Relays in any of the two ways they can connect into your environment - via Windows Authentication Directly to the Datastore or via SQL Authentication directly to the Datastore.</P>
<P><STRONG>Suggested Usage:<BR></STRONG>- If you are reconfiguring a <STRONG>Top Level Relay</STRONG> you should <STRONG>use this fixlet.</STRONG>.<BR>- If you are reconfiguring a <STRONG>Branch Office or Leaf Relay</STRONG> you should use the corresponding Config - RES ONE Workspace Branch Relay - Set Relay Server - Windows Fixlet.</P>
<P><FONT color=#ff0000><STRONG>NOTES: Grayed out settings used in this fixlet are configured via the Environment Configuration section of the Deployment Wizard!</STRONG></FONT><BR>- If you are using <STRONG>"Windows" for authentication</STRONG> the Database Information and Windows Authentication sections below must be populated.<BR>- If you are using <STRONG>"SQL" for authentication</STRONG> the Database Information and SQL Authentication section below must be populated.<BR>

<DIV id=plainOrdinaryFixletDescription>Failed to load parameterized fixlet.</div>
</div>

<script>
    loaded = false;

	function loadGlobalization() {
		var globalization = EvaluateRelevance('(messages of it) of fixlets whose ( name of it = "Parameterized Fixlet Library") of all bes sites whose (name of it = "BES Support")');
		var regex = /\s*<DIV id=globalizationMessageDiv  style="display:none;">([\x00-\x7F]+)\s*<\/Div>/i;
		var matches = regex.exec(globalization);
		var globalizationSanitized = matches[1].replace(/<br>/gi, "");
		return globalizationSanitized;
	}

	function loadUtils() {
		return EvaluateRelevance('unique value of values of mime fields whose (name of it = "vrt_utils.js") of fixlets whose ( name of it = "Parameterized Fixlet Library") of all bes sites whose (name of it = "BES Support")');
	}

    function loadScript(url, callback) {
		var head = document.getElementsByTagName("head")[0];
		var script = document.createElement("script");
		script.type = "text/javascript";
		script.text = loadUtils() + loadGlobalization();
        script.onreadystatechange = callback;
        script.onload = callback;

        head.appendChild(script);
    }

    function scriptLoaded() {
        if (!loaded) {
            var paramFixletDescription = document.getElementById('paramFixletDescription');
            var plainOrdinaryFixletDescription = document.getElementById('plainOrdinaryFixletDescription');

            if (typeof FixletUtils !== 'undefined') {
                loaded = true;
                paramFixletDescription.style.display = "block";
                plainOrdinaryFixletDescription.style.display = "none";

                FixletUtils.initFixletRender();
            } else {
                paramFixletDescription.style.display = "none";
                plainOrdinaryFixletDescription.style.display = "block";
            }
        }
    }

    loadScript("vrt_fixletUtils.js", scriptLoaded);
</script>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>exists relay service OR exists main gather service</Relevance>
    <Relevance>windows of operating system</Relevance>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[version of client >= "9.0"]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance>exists service &quot;RESRLS&quot;</Relevance>
    <Category>Upgrade</Category>
